wingman for Debian
==================

Wingman instances run as the invoking user. Enable linger for a user whose
instances should survive reboot:

    sudo loginctl enable-linger "$USER"

The package grants /usr/bin/netbird CAP_NET_ADMIN, CAP_NET_RAW, and
CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE. A dpkg path trigger reapplies those capabilities whenever
a NetBird package transaction replaces that binary. Removing wingman clears the
capabilities it installed.

The installed polkit rule permits members of Debian's sudo group to configure
systemd-resolved for their rootless NetBird interfaces.
